Q2 – User-Defined Exceptions and Propagation in an Online Examination Portal (7 Marks)
This question focuses on creating custom exceptions in Java, propagating exceptions across multiple layers, and preserving the original cause using exception chaining.

I'll provide the complete Java program, class hierarchy, propagation diagram, Student A and Student B answers, test cases, and complexity analysis.
1. Shared Group Work – Custom Exception Hierarchy
A. Exception hierarchy
We create a parent exception called ExamException and three specific child exceptions.
ExamException

Parent checked exception

ExamWindowClosedException
Exam time expired

StudentNotRegisteredException
Student not enrolled

SubmissionStorageException
File storage failure


All three subclasses are checked exceptions because they extend Exception through ExamException.

B. Why checked exceptions?
Exception	Reason for checked exception
ExamWindowClosedException	Exam closure is a predictable business rule that must be handled.
StudentNotRegisteredException	Registration can be checked and handled by the application.
SubmissionStorageException	Storage failures should be explicitly handled by the calling layer.

Unchecked exceptions are generally suitable for programming mistakes or invalid internal states, such as NullPointerException and IllegalArgumentException.
