B. Demonstrating exception chaining
Exception chaining preserves the original exception inside a new custom exception.
try {
    throw new IOException("Disk quota exceeded");
}
catch (IOException e) {

    throw new SubmissionStorageException(
        "Could not store answer02.pdf", e
    );
}


To access the original exception:
catch (ExamException e) {

    System.out.println(e.getMessage());

    System.out.println(e.getCause().getMessage());

    e.printStackTrace();
}


Possible chained stack trace:
SubmissionStorageException:
Could not store answer02.pdf

Caused by: java.io.IOException:
Disk quota exceeded


The full stack trace also includes the file and line-number information for the exception creation and propagation locations.
